 "unreadable": [],
 "notes": "Districts Karimnagar (cols 14-16), Adilabad (17-19), Medak (20-22), Nizamabad (23-25); table continues from leaf 230 and onto leaf 232. Females printed '..' (nil) for Medak B-(b) Others (P 2, M 2) and Nizamabad A-(c) Others (P 3, M 3); recorded as null. Italic 1 and 4 are hard to tell apart on this page: the italic 4's thin crossbar is often faint, so it looks like a 1. Wherever that glyph appears in a persons figure, printed Males + Females and the sub-totals all show it is a 4, so it is recorded as 4: Karimnagar (b) Indo-European Family and Indo-Aryan Branch 1,144 (final glyph looks most like 1; 600+544; 82+16+1,046); Adilabad Kanarese 10,404; Adilabad (a) Indo-European Family / Indo-Aryan Branch 227,487; Medak Marathi 8,549; Nizamabad Dravida group 6,574; Nizamabad (a) Indo-European Family / Indo-Aryan Branch 67,374; Nizamabad Urdu 45,730 (leading glyph looks like 1). The Karimnagar 1,144 is the least certain; a strict reading could give 1,141. Layout: the Intermediate group (Gondi) is a sub-group of Dravidian Family (in every column Dravidian Family = Andhra + Dravida + Intermediate), so its lang_path includes Dravidian Family. Weakly printed/broken glyphs read with the help of arithmetic: Medak Dravidian Family persons 645,630 (third digit broken, M+F agrees), Medak Urdu persons 76,145 (first digit broken, M+F agrees)."
}